      "writtenOn": "2022-08-05T13:31:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This doesn\u0027t seem to add any value compared to trace_android_rvh_check_preempt_tick(), why is it needed?\n\nAlso, I\u0027m always concerned with these hooks to mess with the preemption rules. Aren\u0027t there locking patterns that could break fairness? What if a task has a locking pattern as follows:\n\nlock(a)\nlock(b)\nunlock(a)\nlock(a)\nunlock(b)\nlock(b)\nunlock(a)\nlock(a)\nunlock(b)\nlock(b)\n...\n\n\nIn this case there is always a lock that has been taken recently, so the task never gets preempted?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4431,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 4433,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "7f83400e5425f8c5fbad6ca06a63dbf8afc9de65",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
